Task: Consumer lag gauge (Phase 4b, ADR 0010).

Added purekafka.consumer.ConsumerLag (record, fromConsumer). Checked
fs2-kafka 3.6.0's real API first (javap against the resolved jar) rather
than assuming an endOffsets method exists - it doesn't; KafkaOffsets/
KafkaOffsetsV2 only expose position/committed. Instead reads Kafka's own
already-tracked per-partition records-lag metric via KafkaMetrics[F].metrics
(wraps the Java client's own consumer.metrics()) - confirmed the exact
metric name (records-lag), group (consumer-fetch-manager-metrics), and
tags (topic, partition) by decompiling kafka-clients' FetchMetricsRegistry/
FetchMetricsManager classes directly, not guessed.

Split into ConsumerLag.record (core polling/gauge-recording logic,
parameterized over F[Map[(String,Int),Double]]) and ConsumerLag.fromConsumer
(the real constructor extracting that map from a live KafkaConsumer) - same
testable-core/real-constructor split DeadLetter.fromPublish/resource
established in Phase 3.

Files: modules/purekafka/src/main/scala/purekafka/consumer/ConsumerLag.scala (new),
modules/purekafka/src/test/scala/purekafka/consumer/ConsumerLagSuite.scala (new).

Tests: 1 new, asserting the gauge records the right value with the right
attributes (topic/partition/group) against a synthetic lag supplier - no
real broker needed. Passes.

Deviation: same as the tracing commit - Red+Green committed together.
